menu "AI engine"

    config AI_ARENA_FAST_KB
        int "Tensor arena for detection and anti-spoof, internal SRAM (KB)"
        default 175
        range 16 2048
        help
            Sized from the SRAM budget of KEHOACH 6.4 and still an estimate:
            E8-T7 measures the real tail and head of each model. Detection
            runs on every frame, so this arena is asked for in internal RAM
            and only falls back to PSRAM, loudly, when it does not fit.

    config AI_ARENA_FAST_HEAD_KB
        int "Split the fast arena, keeping this many KB of activations in SRAM"
        default 0
        range 0 384
        help
            Zero keeps one buffer. Above zero the arena splits: this many KB of
            activations are asked for in internal RAM and the remainder of
            AI_ARENA_FAST_KB holds the persistent half in PSRAM. Worth it when
            the whole arena will not fit internally but its activations will.

    config AI_ARENA_BIG_KB
        int "Tensor arena for recognition, PSRAM (KB)"
        default 512
        range 64 4096
        help
            Recognition runs only after anti-spoof passes, rarely enough to
            live in PSRAM (KEHOACH 3.10). Also an estimate until E8-T7.

    config AI_PROFILING
        bool "Report ticks per operator after every invoke"
        default n
        help
            Turns on TFLM's MicroProfiler, which costs roughly 48 KB of static
            RAM and a print per invoke. E8-T8 uses it to tell an operator with
            an ESP-NN kernel from one running the reference C path.

endmenu
